  "details": "I think for some people it will be more comfortable to use in-game keyboard, instead of opening overlay, selecting window of let's say TTS program and typing in there.\n\nThis would be useful for things such as text-to-speech and translators. \n\nFor example when you have this feature enabled, after clicking \"Send\" button in chatbox window, an OSC message will be sent to TTS program, TTS optionally re-sends it to VRChat(via \"/chatbox/input\") and speaks the message you typed.\n\nAlso would be great if there will be indication that this option is enabled, as people may forget they have this option enabled, so if there's no program which will handle chatbox output - their message will be sent to nowhere.\n\nAlternative implementation may be duplicating the message from chatbox to OSC, instead of redirecting it",
